specs\_codex-impl-delivery-live-card-2026-05-19.log:1260:specs\new-arch\2026-05-16-overlay-message-turn-agent-cards.md:475:2. Integrity review events remain a protocol exception in P1. Backend `integrity.review.started`, `integrity.review.progress`, `integrity.review.chunk`, and `integrity.review.completed` carry `sessionID` but do not carry a durable `messageID`; `started/progress/chunk` can arrive before any message metadata for that integrity session. Therefore the overlay keeps the existing single `integrity:session:<sessionID>` card for `integrity.review.*` protocol events rather than inventing a synthetic message id. If the backend later emits integrity verdict/progress as normal `message.updated` / `message.part.updated` rows with real message ids, this exception must be removed and integrity must route through the standard message-turn mechanism.
